      "modern_form": "PIE *h₁rewgʰ-m(e)n- / *réwgʰ-no-s 'cream, butter' — Pokorny 'reugh-m(e)n- ,Rahm^?' IEW 873 (NOT 837)",
      "note": "Two things to separate. (1) The root label and gloss are essentially right: Pokorny does have an entry 'reugh-m(e)n- ,Rahm^?' whose whole content is 'Av. raoγna- ,Butter^, mpers. npers. rōγan ,(ausgelassene) Butter^; aisl. rjúmi m. ,Rahm^, ablautend ags. rēam, mnd. rōme, ahd. roum ,Sahne^ ...'. But Pokorny writes it with a question mark, and his own source Walde-Pokorny II 357 f. calls the whole equation 'höchst unsicher' and prefers to take the Germanic 'cream' words from *reu- 'aufreißen' (*reu-, rou-, ru-m(en)- 'skin, layer of fat on milk', after Fick); Buck (§5.89 BUTTER) says of Av. raoγna- 'outside connections unknown'. Modern reconstruction keeps the Iranian side but derives it as *rewgʰ- + *-nos ('*réwgʰ-no-s'), i.e. an n-stem, not an -men- stem. So: Iranian branch certain, Germanic branch doubtful, hence 'plausible' rather than 'confirmed'. (2) The page reference POK:837 is wrong: p.837 of IEW is in the *pleu- 'to flow, swim' article (POK_03.txt leaf 72); the reugh-m(e)n- entry stands on p.873. Nourai's digits are transposed (873 → 837); the same wrong number is repeated on node #1. Aryanpur's parallel entry cites Pokorny too and Wiktionary cites 'IEW p. 873'.",
