          "derivation": "Avestan raoγna- (neuter) 'butter' is securely attested — Bartholomae quotes it from Hādōxt Nask 2.18, where zarǝmaya- raoγna- 'spring butter' is the food of the blessed, and gives the adjective raoγnavant- 'having butter' (Vd. 21.7) and the feminine raoγnyā- 'butter' (Yt. 12.3). It continues Proto-Iranian *ráwgnah, an -as-stem built on *rawgʰ-na- ; Bartholomae himself adds 'Ableit. — np. rōγan „ausgelassene Butter“. Pü.: rōγn'. Nourai's gloss 'oil' follows Darmesteter (Buck records both renderings, 'butter' per Bartholomae, 'oil' per Darmesteter); either is defensible, since the word covers clarified fat. The ONLY defect is the page number: POK:837 should be POK:873.",
